<h4>C. The Decision Tree</h4>
<p>Draw a tree. On the trunk write your name. On the roots write what sustains you: your faith, your family, your values. On the branches write the decisions you have made recently. Color the branches green for free decisions toward the good; color them brown for impulsive or enslaving decisions. At the end, write one sentence from the lesson that summarizes what you have learned about freedom.</p>

<h4>D. Letter from a Freed Slave</h4>
<p>Imagine you have been enslaved for years by something (a vice, a resentment, a fear). One day Christ frees you. Write a letter of gratitude to Jesus, telling him what your life was like in slavery and what it is like now in freedom. (6-8 lines)</p>
